# Whether the exiled card's owner could cast it is judged for the owner, not the Queller's controller (CR 608.2g, 101.2).
# Bot1 controls Drannith Magistrate ("Your opponents can't cast spells from anywhere other than their hands") and Spell
# Queller, which exiles Bot2's Lightning Bolt. When Bot2's second Bolt kills the Queller, Bot2 - an opponent of the
# Magistrate's controller - can't cast the exiled Bolt from exile, so is not asked (the refusal); judged for Bot1, who may
# cast from exile, it would be. The Bolt stays in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Drannith Magistrate
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Spell Queller
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x2
Lightning Bolt x2
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Drannith Magistrate.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spell Queller.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile = Lightning Bolt
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Spell Queller)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot2.Accept
[Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Spell Queller; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Drannith Magistrate.Tapped = false
Bot1.Life = 20
